    "did_you_know": "This simple but elegant abstracted landscape was shot in Jutland, Denmark.",
    "description": "Toni Schneiders was part of the Subjective Photography movement in Germany. While its members produced straight photographs that depicted the external world, their goal was to create images that elicited subjective interpretation and emphasized emotional and intellectual reactions over factual information. “If I succeed in making visible only a little of the magic of light and a touch of poetry in my pictures, this is luck enough for me,” said Schneiders.",
